NAME
     useradd - add and change users and groups

SYNOPSIS
     useradd [-u UID] [-g GROUP] [-G GROUPS] [-d DIR] [-s SHELL] [-m] NAME
     userdel [-r] NAME
     usermod [-u UID] [-g GROUP] [-G GROUPS] [-d DIR] [-s SHELL] [-L|-U] NAME
     groupadd [-g GID] NAME
     groupdel NAME
     groupmod [-g GID] [-n NEWNAME] NAME

DESCRIPTION
     One program under six names, which together edit /etc/passwd,
     /etc/group and /etc/shadow. Each writes to a temporary file and
     renames it, so an interrupted change leaves the old file.

OPTIONS
     -u UID      the user id
     -g GROUP    the primary group
     -G GROUPS   the supplementary groups
     -d DIR      the home directory
     -s SHELL    the login shell
     -m          make the home directory
     -r          userdel: remove the home directory too
     -L, -U      usermod: lock or unlock the account
     -n NEWNAME  groupmod: rename

SEE ALSO
     passwd(1), login(1), id(1)
